<title>JAPAN: Japan April domestic vehicle output up 11.4% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan April domestic vehicle output up 11.4% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's domestic vehicle production rose 11.4 percent in April from a year earlier to 887,150 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers Association said on Monday.  </p>
<p>It was the second consecutive month of year-on-year growth.</p>
<p>The association said it expected exports in April to have risen about 19 percent from a year earlier. It will announce official export figures on May 28.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of figures in April, with percentage changes:</p>
<p>				     April	    YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Cars			     689,832	   up   15.5</p>
<p> Trucks			   191,419	   down  1.9</p>
<p> Buses				5,899	   up   40.1</p>
<p>April production by five major manufacturers with percentage changes:</p>
<p>				     April		YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Toyota Motor	290,675	   up    8.1</p>
<p> Nissan Motor	135,542	   up   17.8</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 107,771	   up   23.3</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors  93,742	   up   15.1</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	  70,022	   up   12.4</p>
